<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kandy</h1><p class="st-meta">1469 CE – 1815 CE (approx.) · capital Kandy</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last independent kingdom of Sri Lanka, which kept the Portuguese, Dutch and British at bay in its central highlands for three centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a>, in the central highlands, began as a sub-kingdom of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kotte">Kingdom of Kotte</a> in the later 15th century, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senasammata-vikramabahu">Senasammata Vikramabahu</a>. After the Portuguese arrival it became a refuge of Sinhalese independence, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vimaladharmasuriya-i">Vimaladharmasuriya I</a> secured its throne in the 1590s, defeating a Portuguese army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-danture">Danture</a> in 1594.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kings guarded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/relic-of-the-tooth-of-the-buddha">Tooth Relic</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-of-the-tooth">Temple of the Tooth</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a>, the symbol of Sinhalese kingship. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasinha-ii-of-kandy">Rajasinha II</a> allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> to expel the Portuguese. From 1739 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaks-of-kandy">Nayak</a> kings of south Indian origin ruled, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kirti-sri-rajasinha">Kirti Sri Rajasinha</a> revived the Buddhist monastic order with monks from Siam. The hill country relied on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> and areca, while forests and mountains defended it.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Discontent among Kandyan nobles against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-vikrama-rajasinha">Sri Vikrama Rajasinha</a> allowed British forces to enter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a> in 1815. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandyan-convention">Kandyan Convention</a> transferred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> to the British Crown, and the kingdom became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-ceylon">British Ceylon</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-kandy.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Kandy" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Janith (talk) 03:45, 16 August 2008 (UTC) Original uploader was Uvants2 at en.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_of_Kandy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1469 CE – 1815 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kandy</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vimaladharmasuriya I, Rajasinha II, Sri Vikrama Rajasinha</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sinhala</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kandyan Kingdom, Kingdom of Senkadagala, Kanda Uda Rata</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1642&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kandy" aria-label="Kingdom of Kandy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6911 1905 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Kandy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7231 2161L7211 2175M7231 2161L7212 2176"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7211 2175h0M7212 2176h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7231 2161h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7231 2161h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kandy. <a href="/atlas?year=1642&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kandy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
